1. Circular proof of the core deliverable remains unresolved. Lines 64-75 and 172/201 let `#2045` serve as both the subject under change and one of the “validated real plan” exemplars, while `test_issue_2045_example_plans.sh` only checks headings/placeholders. That does not prove “real plans that demonstrate template usage and review conventions”; it proves formatting. This is a substantive acceptance gap, not a wording issue.
2. The operational acceptance still depends on live issue state instead of a stable repo-owned invariant. Lines 129-133, 176, and 203 require current comments/labels on GitHub issue `#2045`. That can fail because of label churn, auth state, API availability, or later workflow changes unrelated to the code change. The plan still does not define execution prerequisites or a fallback, so the criterion is not reliably falsifiable.

